---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Best Budget Cigar Starter Kits | StickScore Guides"
  description="What a beginner setup actually needs to cost, piece by piece — we don't yet track pre-bundled kits, so here's the honest breakdown."
>
  <div class="home-hero">
    <div class="cigar-hero__eyebrow">Buying Guide</div>
    <h1 class="home-hero__title">Best Budget Cigar Starter Kits</h1>
  </div>

  <section class="section summary-review">
    <p>
      A quick note before this one: we don't yet have pre-bundled "starter kit" products in our
      database — most bundled kits sold by retailers mix and match individual pieces we do track,
      often at a discount versus buying separately, but we haven't independently verified specific
      bundle pricing yet. What follows is the honest breakdown of what a beginner setup actually
      needs, piece by piece, so you can judge whether a bundle you're looking at is a real deal.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section__heading">The four essentials</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>A humidor.</strong> See <a href="/guides/best-humidors-under-100/">humidors under
      $100</a> — a decent one doesn't require spending more than that starting out.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>A cutter.</strong> See <a href="/guides/best-cigar-cutters/">best cigar cutters</a>
      and <a href="/guides/guillotine-vs-v-cut-vs-punch/">which cut style to pick</a> if you're
      unsure. A basic guillotine is the safest default for a first cutter.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>A lighter.</strong> See <a href="/guides/best-torch-lighters/">best torch
      lighters</a> — a single-jet torch is plenty for a first lighter; you don't need a quad-torch
      to start.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>A hygrometer</strong> (if your humidor doesn't include a reliable one) — see
      <a href="/guides/best-hygrometers/">best hygrometers</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section__heading">What a bundle typically saves you</h2>
    <p>
      Pre-bundled kits usually combine a mid-range humidor with a basic cutter and lighter at a
      modest discount versus buying each separately — but "basic" often means the included cutter
      or lighter is the cheapest option in the bundle-maker's lineup, not necessarily good value on
      its own. Compare the bundle's included pieces against our individual category guides above
      before assuming the bundle is the better deal.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section__heading">If you're buying piece by piece instead</h2>
    <p>
      There's no real downside to buying the four essentials separately rather than as a kit — you
      get to choose the cut style and lighter type you actually want, rather than whatever came
      bundled. It just takes a bit more research, which is exactly what the guides above are for.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
